## Design credits

Before implementing `packages/session-delete`, we read a number of community DSH plugins that also
delete sessions. What we took from them is **design and sequencing, not code**. No source code from
the projects below has been copied into this repository, so their copyright notices and license
texts are not reproduced here: no such obligation has been triggered yet. If code is ever adopted
from one of them, the corresponding notice and license text will be added to this file verbatim.

| Project | License | Design we borrowed |
| ------- | ------- | ------------------ |
| [Jaylor-Wang/dsh-tool-session-delete](https://github.com/Jaylor-Wang/dsh-tool-session-delete) | MIT | Deletion ordering: archive first (which closes the provider `agent/pre-step` gate), then stop activity, flush, settle, and only then move the log directory out. Also the plain-JS `declareRemote()` pattern for registering Typert remote methods, because V8 decorators are unavailable in this runtime. |
| [xohmai/dsh-session-delete](https://github.com/xohmai/dsh-session-delete) | Apache-2.0 | Trash layout: a dedicated trash root outside the session tree, one directory per operation with a `meta.json`, and an append-only `audit.log` in JSONL. Also the idea of reconciling "archived in the workspace state but gone from disk" ghost entries. |
| [DDDMUC/dsh-delete-session](https://github.com/DDDMUC/dsh-delete-session) | MIT | The problem framing: prove that no writer is active before touching session files, and treat `EBUSY` / `EPERM` on the directory as a retryable state. We deliberately did **not** adopt its write-lease probe (`open(id, "write")`): that call publishes a new log generation on historical sessions (see [`docs/adr/0004-session-delete-architecture.md`](docs/adr/0004-session-delete-architecture.md) §6), so this plugin uses read-only liveness signals and retries the move on busy instead. |
| [Lzcdebear/better-dsh-session-deletetool](https://github.com/Lzcdebear/better-dsh-session-deletetool) | MIT | Lineage-based identification of sub-sessions and forks (subagent catalog plus `SessionHeader.parentSession`), used to count related sessions in the delete plan. |

## Design credits（session-rewind）

| Project | License | Design we borrowed |
| ------- | ------- | ------------------ |
| [SiriLee/dsh-rewind](https://github.com/SiriLee/dsh-rewind) | MIT | The in-place rewind mechanism: append one `user/message` marker whose `surfaceOp` replaces the target and every later surface node, keep the log append-only, hide the withdrawn rows in the client by wrapping the registered Chat view builder with `visibility: "hidden"`, and inject the ↶ action into the official message action row by taking over the `conversation.chat.node` slot entry. We read its source to verify these seams exist; the implementation here is independent plain JavaScript and no source code was copied. |

## 中文摘要（session-rewind）

写 `packages/session-rewind` 之前，我们读了 [SiriLee/dsh-rewind](https://github.com/SiriLee/dsh-rewind)（MIT，241★）。
**只借鉴架构，没有复制代码**：确认了两条关键 seam ——「向日志追加一条 `surfaceOp: replace` 的
`user/message` 标记」可以只截断模型可见上下文而不动历史；「包装已注册的 Chat builder，把节点标成
`visibility: "hidden"`」可以让被撤回的行从渲染对话里消失，同时保留在节点 store 里供输入框回填；
以及接管 `conversation.chat.node` 的 user 渲染器、往官方 actions 行的 `extraActions` 里塞按钮的
消息动作注入方式。本仓库的实现是独立的 plain JS（无构建、无 TypeScript），若将来真的复制其代码，
会在本文件逐字补上版权与许可全文。

## 中文摘要

写 `packages/session-delete` 之前，我们读过上面四个 MIT / Apache-2.0 社区插件（Jaylor-Wang、xohmai、DDDMUC、Lzcdebear）。**只借鉴设计，没有复制代码**，对应关系：

- 删除时序（先归档、再停活、flush、settle，最后移走日志目录），以及 plain JS 手工登记 remote 方法的写法 —— Jaylor-Wang；
- 回收站目录布局、`meta.json` 与 `audit.log` 结构、归档幽灵的核对思路 —— xohmai；
- 「先证明没有活写者再动文件」的问题意识与遇忙重试 —— DDDMUC（实现上没有采用它的 write-open 租约探测，见 ADR 0004 §6）；
- 用血缘判定子会话 / fork 的思路 —— Lzcdebear。

因为没有复制代码，本文件不附它们的版权声明与许可全文；一旦真的复制，会在此处逐字补上对应的版权与许可条款。
